{"parentUuid":"c60e5071-6fe9-4ade-b783-e122585f832c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a9d8ba25a087fb653","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AAPvpnT6JuVQpuhYm4KxUo","type":"tool_result","content":"# Four Valley Infrastructure Design Philosophy\n\nBased on the guide, the core layout principles for Valley Four's infrastructure include:\n\n**Modular Production Lines**\nThe guide emphasizes \"equal-width full-speed operation\" across multiple specialized production chains: Qiaoyu capsules, refined variants, Gaogu batteries, and crystal shells. Each module maintains consistent throughput metrics.\n\n**Resource Allocation Strategy**\nThe design balances supply with demand: \"紫晶矿的产量与市场需求完全一致，确保供应稳定\" (mineral production aligns with market demand to ensure stable supply). The system deliberately diverts surplus source ore—20 units per minute—toward crystal shell production.\n\n**Power Management**\nThe infrastructure uses one standard power plant plus four speed-restricted generators consuming 6.5 batteries per minute. This configuration reflects optimization for \"电力需求为505单位\" (power requirements of 505 units per minute) across equipment layouts.\n\n**Quantifiable Metrics**\nDaily output targets include: 34,560 capsules, 25,920 refined variants, 16,560 batteries, and 28,800 crystal shells—generating over 4 million dispatch vouchers daily through efficient production orchestration.\n\nThe philosophy prioritizes **density and efficiency** through systematic resource balancing rather than speculative over-building."}]},"uuid":"0ddebc84-f580-40ff-bcbf-42001dd9db8a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:11.703Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c60e5071-6fe9-4ade-b783-e122585f832c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9efe9f7b-cd62-4ade-b479-26a1667f62a1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a9d8ba25a087fb653","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018RfocfMV17Qd64Td1HZznV","type":"tool_result","content":"# 《明日方舟终末地》工业布局核心设计哲学\n\n## 基础设计原则\n\n该攻略强调**现地加工优于中央集中**的理念。核心逻辑是：\"总线尽可能输出原材料，在现场一路加工成成品\"，因为将中间产物存入仓库需消耗额外总线出口槽位，而基地面积充足但总线容量有限。\n\n## 关键端口走向技巧\n\n**先消耗总线末端**是效率优化的关键。靠近拐角的总线最难有效利用，从边角开始铺设可避免格子计算错误。**协议储存箱替代输入总线**能显著节省总线空间——通过无线传输实现灵活布局。\n\n## 动力杆放置经验\n\n不追求供电范围最大化。作者建议\"哪里没电了直接拍一个\"，因为电线杆成本低廉，占用的边角空间通常无他用。在研磨机-精炼-粉碎集群中，紧贴粉碎输出口放置可极限供电。\n\n## 必避坑点\n\n- **物流桥导致卡顿**：经过两个物流桥会产生约四个产物的延迟\n- **共用协议储存箱问题**：易爆仓产物与重要产物混放会卡产线\n- **装备产线冗余**：仅保留当前最高等级一条，低级装备无实用价值\n\n## 总线-空间均衡哲学\n\n主基地总线槽位相对稀缺，据点则相反。此设计体现\"用劣质空间换取总线容量利用\"的权衡——通过协议储存箱中转实现灵活调度。"}]},"uuid":"aa6c5a8e-b8b1-4c66-9d22-2e96329ba318","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:12.318Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9efe9f7b-cd62-4ade-b479-26a1667f62a1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c17b777f-0790-44af-8965-2bc13631d92e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a9d8ba25a087fb653","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fj1aR2Kk14WzznJqXmQGC6","type":"tool_result","content":"# AIC Factory Blueprint Design Patterns - Limited Information\n\nBased on the provided content, I cannot fully address your request about design patterns in top blueprints. The article focuses on **where to find blueprints and their benefits** rather than analyzing their structural characteristics.\n\n## What the Article Does Cover:\n\nThe content mentions that effective blueprints include:\n- \"one well-fed packaging unit can maintain multiple Thermal Banks, producing enough energy to keep a big layout running\"\n- Power setup considerations using Thermal Banks and batteries\n- Input requirements (Iron Ore, Originium Ore, Ferrium, etc.)\n\n## Critical Gap:\n\nThe article **does not discuss**:\n- Footprint dimensions or aspect ratios\n- Power pole placement conventions\n- Storage box positioning strategies\n- Port direction standards\n- Design anti-patterns to avoid\n\n## Recommendation:\n\nTo extract the specific design patterns you're seeking, you would need to:\n1. Access the actual blueprints through in-game AIC interface\n2. Explore community sites mentioned: Talos Pioneers or Endfield Tools\n3. Review Reddit threads linked in the article (like the r/Endfield layout discussion)\n\nThese sources would contain visual layouts showing the structural conventions you're asking about."}]},"uuid":"d0c6a087-db24-4c40-a472-e806c9feee62","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:15.239Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c17b777f-0790-44af-8965-2bc13631d92e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
